From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sliva0 <sliva0mk@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 14:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Diameter: Rename IP-Bit-Mask-Width to IP-Mask-Bit-Mask-Width

RFC 5777's verified erratum 2335 (global) corrects every
IP-Bit-Mask-Width to IP-Mask-Bit-Mask-Width: "Since the AVP is referred
as IP-Mask-Bit-Mask-Width in the IANA registry, this name should be
used." Clause 4.1.7.7's heading and the allocation table in section
10.1 give AVP 523 that name too; the IANA AVP Codes registry lists it.

The entry was named IP-Mask-Bit-Mask-Width when it was added and was
renamed to match the IP-Address-Mask member, which follows the RFC's
uncorrected ABNF; both are renamed here. Renaming an AVP renames its
display filter field (diameter.IP-Bit-Mask-Width becomes
diameter.IP-Mask-Bit-Mask-Width), so saved filters and profiles using
the old name need updating.
---
 resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
index 56a8586..c3f8542 100644
--- a/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
+++ b/resources/protocols/diameter/dictionary.xml
@@ -2357,10 +2357,10 @@
 		<avp name="IP-Address-Mask" code="522" mandatory="must" may-encrypt="no" protected="mustnot" vendor-bit="mustnot">
 			<grouped>
 				<gavp name="IP-Address"/>
-				<gavp name="IP-Bit-Mask-Width"/>
+				<gavp name="IP-Mask-Bit-Mask-Width"/>
 			</grouped>
 		</avp>
-		<avp name="IP-Bit-Mask-Width" code="523" mandatory="may">
+		<avp name="IP-Mask-Bit-Mask-Width" code="523" mandatory="may">
 			<type type-name="Unsigned32"/>
 		</avp>
 		<avp name="MAC-Address" code="524" mandatory="may">
